# Aurelia Browser - files whose bytes are part of the build contract.
#
# Every patch in chromium/patches carries the sha256 of its own bytes in its
# .meta.json, and `node tools/chromium/cli.mjs verify-patches` recomputes that
# digest from the checked-out file before it will let a build start. Any
# line-ending conversion changes the bytes, so a Windows checkout made with
# core.autocrlf=true produced CRLF patch files that matched neither their
# recorded digest nor the unified-diff grammar - while the same checkout on
# Linux passed both, and the same patch set verified cleanly against upstream.
#
# `text eol=lf` pins the checkout to LF on every platform and overrides
# core.autocrlf, so the bytes on disk are the bytes in the repository no
# matter how the machine that cloned it is configured.
chromium/patches/*.patch text eol=lf
chromium/patches/*.meta.json text eol=lf
